@anon.42b86dac05eb578258e9e0f4074366cb.156 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [940 x i8] }> <{ [940 x i8] c"Overrides to apply when resolving the project's dependencies.\0A\0AOverrides are used to force selection of a specific version of a package, regardless of the\0Aversion requested by any other package, and regardless of whether choosing that version\0Awould typically constitute an invalid resolution.\0A\0AWhile constraints are _additive_, in that they're combined with the requirements of the\0Aconstituent packages, overrides are _absolute_, in that they completely replace the\0Arequirements of any constituent packages.\0A\0AIncluding a package as an override will _not_ trigger installation of the package on its\0Aown; instead, the package must be requested elsewhere in the project's first-party or\0Atransitive dependencies.\0A\0A!!! note\0A    In `uv lock`, `uv sync`, and `uv run`, uv will only read `override-dependencies` from\0A    the `pyproject.toml` at the workspace root, and will ignore any declarations in other\0A    workspace members or `uv.toml` files." }>, align 1
