@anon.42b86dac05eb578258e9e0f4074366cb.191 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [319 x i8] }> <{ [319 x i8] c"The sources to use when resolving dependencies.\0A\0A`tool.uv.sources` enriches the dependency metadata with additional sources, incorporated during development. A dependency source can be a Git repository, a URL, a local path, or an alternative registry.\0A\0ASee [Dependencies](../concepts/projects/dependencies.md) for more." }>, align 1
@anon.42b86dac05eb578258e9e0f4074366cb.192 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1203 x i8] }> <{ [1203 x i8] c"The indexes to use when resolving dependencies.\0A\0AAccepts either a repository compliant with [PEP 503](https://peps.python.org/pep-0503/) (the simple repository API), or a local directory laid out in the same format.\0A\0AIndexes are considered in the order in which they're defined, such that the first-defined index has the highest priority. Further, the indexes provided by this setting are given higher priority than any indexes specified via [`index_url`](#index-url) or [`extra_index_url`](#extra-index-url). uv will only consider the first index that contains a given package, unless an alternative [index strategy](#index-strategy) is specified.\0A\0AIf an index is marked as `explicit = true`, it will be used exclusively for the dependencies that select it explicitly via `[tool.uv.sources]`, as in:\0A\0A```toml [[tool.uv.index]] name = \22pytorch\22 url = \22https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\22 explicit = true\0A\0A[tool.uv.sources] torch = { index = \22pytorch\22 } ```\0A\0AIf an index is marked as `default = true`, it will be moved to the end of the prioritized list, such that it is given the lowest priority when resolving packages. Additionally, marking an index as default will disable the PyPI default index." }>, align 1
@anon.42b86dac05eb578258e9e0f4074366cb.193 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [49 x i8] }> <{ [49 x i8] c"The workspace definition for the project, if any." }>, align 1
@anon.42b86dac05eb578258e9e0f4074366cb.194 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [102 x i8] }> <{ [102 x i8] c"Whether the project is managed by uv. If `false`, uv will ignore the project when `uv run` is invoked." }>, align 1
@anon.42b86dac05eb578258e9e0f4074366cb.195 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [541 x i8] }> <{ [541 x i8] c"Whether the project should be considered a Python package, or a non-package (\22virtual\22) project.\0A\0APackages are built and installed into the virtual environment in editable mode and thus require a build backend, while virtual projects are _not_ built or installed; instead, only their dependencies are included in the virtual environment.\0A\0ACreating a package requires that a `build-system` is present in the `pyproject.toml`, and that the project adheres to a structure that adheres to the build backend's expectations (e.g., a `src` layout)." }>, align 1
